// Fixture: multi_file_test, file 1 of 5 (see HANDOFF.md for the full
// combination order and what each cross-file reference direction
// exercises).
//
// Deliberately a non-.gddl extension (.weapon) -- proves §18.3's
// "no assumed extension" claim is real, not just asserted. This file
// must be named explicitly on the CLI or via a pattern that doesn't
// assume .gddl; an unqualified extension-agnostic pattern (items/*)
// or an explicit .weapon pattern both work.
//
// Sword references Weapon (define, in weapon_type.gddl, LATER in
// combination order -- a FORWARD reference) and Element.fire
// (identifier, in elements.gddl, also LATER -- a FORWARD identifier
// reference). Both must resolve correctly per §18.2's confirmed
// forward-reference behavior.

Weapon Sword
	damage  = 10
	element = Element.fire
